  <h2>ASCII Table</h2>
  <p>ASCII (American Standard Code for Information Interchange) is a character encoding standard that maps integers (0–127) to text characters. It includes uppercase and lowercase Latin letters, digits, punctuation marks, and control characters. The table below shows every ASCII character with its decimal, hexadecimal, octal, and binary representation.</p>

